/** Part 2 — beur-hagra, tiferet-yisrael, torat-hashlamim, turei-zahav */
export const PART2 = {
  'beur-hagra': {
    '2#א': `How she fixes it, etc. Tosafot 64a s.v. itmar, etc.; and Tosafot Bava Kamma 37b s.v. day, etc.; and several places, etc. (Likut) How, etc. From what is stated in mishnah there 63b "she was accustomed," etc. "she changed three times," etc. — evidently she must triple in intervals; and it challenged there 64a "it established her accustomed," etc. "what does it call her accustomed — behold necessarily accustomed from mishnah"; and further from what we teach afterward "a woman does not fix," etc. — evidently no distinction between establishment of this accustomed one and another not accustomed. Tosafot HaRosh; and Tosafot Bava Kamma 37b s.v. day, etc. And even though they said there 63b "Shmuel said they said," etc. — that is per Rabbi, as Tosafot there s.v. for days, etc., and as stated in Gemara; and that which says there "this is R. Gamliel's words," etc. — he holds they disputed there 64a Rav and Shmuel and said until she triples, etc.; and likewise anonymous mishnah there like Rashbag; and decided explicitly in chapter HaBa al haYevamah (64b) like Rashbag in vesetot. Tosafot HaRosh; and Tosafot 63b s.v. this, etc.; and one version s.v. she jumped, etc. (end quote).`,
    '3#_': `If she fixed, etc. From what is stated 63b: it was taught how R. Yosi — days and hours and veset, etc. — appears specifically days and hours; and as stated from day twenty to day twenty, etc. In this R. Yehuda disputes R. Yosi specifically; and Shmuel 66a "for then," etc. "and the Baalei," etc. — because it precedes the hour she was accustomed to come home and immersion is not on a fixed day.`,
    '5#_': `Sometimes, etc. Tosafot 64a s.v. itmar, etc. And it appears even though Tosafot wrote for all — nevertheless for Shmuel we need five; and here it is per Rav and the latter reasoning in seif 7; and so Shach — see there.`,
    '6#ב': `Even though, etc. There in Tosafot; and likewise Raavad inferred from that they call skipping in dispute of Rav and Shmuel; and Rosh there; and Avodat HaGoren.`,
    '8#_': `She saw, etc. Tosafot s.v. the above; and R. Chananel, etc.`,
    '9#_': `She saw, etc. As stated chapter 4 of Bava Kamma (37a) "he saw an ox gored an ox and did not gore," etc.; and there (b) "deceives for vesetot" as stated in dispute, etc.; and fixed here three times like there; and seif 12.`,
    '12#_': `Alternation veset, etc. As stated above seif 9; and with this the difficulty of Tosafot s.v. the above is resolved "and therefore difficulty," etc. And per this Perishah in name of Raavad "what is this interval unlike," etc. — see there.`,
    '13#א': `The woman, etc. All this as stated above seif 2 and as stated in mishnah and Gemara.`,
    '17#א': `Every veset, etc. Per Tosafot there s.v. rather, etc.; and see there 63b s.v. she ate, etc.; and one can say, etc.; and likewise Rashba decided in Tosafot HaRosh — see there 173a; and so R. Chananel and Shitah Mekubetzet; but Raavad and Tur like Rashi.`,
    '17#ב': `She jumped and saw, etc. In the latter version and he explains he disputes the first version; but all poskim wrote he does not dispute the first version — in the latter version it deals where she did not jump at all on Shabbat; and what is in our version in the latter version on Shabbat she jumped and I did not see — is a scribal error; and from Rambam's words it was copied; but it is not so, for in all their versions it is not present; but Rambam explains the latter version also like the first — that she jumped and saw; but Rosh and Rashba and Shitah Mekubetzet wrote they do not dispute these versions; and likewise anonymous below seif 2.`,
    '19#ג': `And all these, etc. Meaning she fixes even without days and not for jumps that are due to coercion; and proof from what is stated "she was accustomed," etc. "R. Yosi also days and hours," etc. — appears initially without days; therefore R. Yosi and R. Yehuda dispute there — see there 63; and greater than this Tosafot there s.v. she ate, etc.; and one can say, etc.`,
    '20#_': `She yawned, etc. but, etc. As stated above seif 17 that they explain they do not dispute these versions against each other.`,
    '23#א': `She ate, etc. Gemara there; and Beit Yosef wrote from Rosh's and Mordechai's words it appears by three types of eating she fixed veset. His words are puzzling, for Rosh's language is like Gemara's and in Mordechai appears the opposite — he wrote in siman 17 "all day forbidden to have relations," etc. "but a woman whose veset is for days but for other signs," etc. "she yawned sneezed," etc. "or ate garlic or ate peppers," etc.; and so in Tosafot HaRosh 168b; and there is accustomed to see in compound days — and action how: e.g. she jumped on one Shabbat and saw and jumped on one Shabbat and saw, or ate peppers on one Shabbat and saw and ate peppers on one Shabbat and saw, etc.; therefore poskim omitted it included in law of jumps and hold like Rashba that it is not fixed except in days like law of jumps; and Gemara did not mention there except to divide between them and other vesetot that are on one and two; and this is in three; but for us all is in three since decided like Rashbag in chapter HaBa al haYevamah — no need for this.`,
    '23#ב': `And some say, etc. As above — view of Rashba and Shitah Mekubetzet.`,
    '27#א': `Even if she brought forth, etc. and likewise, etc. As stated 66a "before twelve years they are presumptive," etc.; and without bringing forth even afterward she is a minor; and even at age twenty; and as stated 67b; and Shmuel; and not like Rashi there 5a s.v. we are not concerned — in one of them suffices; and language "when they reached" is strained; and it is not so, for explicitly taught in Tosafeta ch. 1 "when she brought two hairs." Tosafot HaRosh. And Rashi explains there deals before twelve years; and this is Rashi's intent in one of them.`,
    '27#ב': `If they examined her, etc. As stated 66a "the halachah is we are concerned," etc. "this is," etc. "and likewise," etc. "and specifically if they examined her; but otherwise presumption," etc. as stated; and Avodat HaGoren siman 255.`,
    '27#ד': `Except there is a distinction, etc. There 9b "passed over her," etc. "unlike all other women for we do not rule like R. Eliezer in mishnah who said every woman," etc.; and as stated 9b "they taught incident and Rabbi acted like R. Eliezer," etc. "unlike a minor girl," etc. "for even Rabbanan agree," etc. "only from end 'her time came to see' I say the end," etc.; and Rashi there s.v. I say the end, etc.`,
    '28#_': `And likewise an elderly woman, etc. There; and as stated above 133; and likewise minor and elderly woman — all who did not fix veset — are like pregnant and nursing as stated in mishnah; and no distinction among them except second sighting as stated in 161; and as stated; and in what they said, etc. as stated 10b "language — except virgin and elderly woman," etc.; if so no relevance for vesetot except elderly woman who ceased three onot as stated 9b; and in virgin no relevance at all except without reaching to see as above; and Tosafot there 9b s.v. elderly woman, etc.; but virgin who reached to see — not as stated in Gemara "and when her time came," etc. "passed," etc.; and we establish like R. Eliezer specifically as above.`,
    '31#_': `She returned, etc. As stated in mishnah there and in what they said, etc. "but," etc. "and elderly woman" refers to that section; and as Tosafot there s.v. elderly woman, etc.; therefore they did not need to ask she again sees in onot — only regarding minor; and this is what is written "and with this," etc.`,
    '32#א': `Sometimes, etc. 64d 39b; and Tosafot there s.v. evidently, etc. And it appears to explain it deals, etc.`,
    '32#ב': `And fourth on 20th of month, etc. So it should read; and it is Raavad's words; and Shach; and Raavad follows his view that rules even nowadays like Gemara law that woman does not fix veset in zivah days as stated 39a-b; therefore he said on 20th except Rosh Chodesh is on 11th to 20th; therefore he said she fixed initially on Rosh Chodesh; and as Raavad wrote: even though initially she does not fix, nevertheless afterward it is not uprooted until uprooted twice; and this is what is written "and fourth on 20th of month and Rosh Chodesh," etc. But Ramban and Rashba in Tosafot HaRosh and Tur already decided nowadays always fixes veset for daughters of Israel were stringent on themselves not to need to learn gates of niddah and zivah; if so you still require her to teach them; therefore nine sightings and six suffice three times on Rosh Chodesh and wrote for month or before.`,
    '33#א': `Pregnant, etc. and nursing, etc. From what is stated 10b "all days of pregnancy she is presumptive," etc.; and there "they were flowing and coming she is presumptive," etc. — appears even if she saw several times; and so Tosafot there s.v. she is presumptive, etc.; and Shmuel and R. Yochanan — even though R. Yosi and R. Shimon dispute R. Meir — nevertheless since R. Yochanan and Shmuel hold like R. Meir so we rule; and as stated we do not follow dispute of Tannaim where Amoraim dispute; and likewise R. Yosi in mishnah who said pregnant and nursing who passed, etc. — we also do not rule like him; and even though Tanna Kama preceded there 10b "he opened," etc. "that Tanna comes," etc.; and likewise R. Yochanan there 9a; and this is Raavad's view; and Ramban disputes and wrote she fixed in nursing days from what is stated 11b "one taught examine lest," etc. "it works out," etc.; and Rashba rejected and assessed that is per R. Yehuda and R. Yosi and R. Shimon who hold on all of them; and we rule like R. Meir — see there 171b where he extended.`,
    '33#ג': `Nevertheless she is concerned, etc. Tosafot HaRosh in name of Raavad; and he wrote like on 11th day per R. Pinchas there 39a-b who said she is concerned even though not fixed; and Raavad follows his view ruling like R. Pinchas and his reason from what is stated 68b "R. Huna son of R. Huna said when we say," etc. "and if we say she is not concerned it is as if non-existent"; and Rashba wrote but Shitah Mekubetzet ruled like R. Huna son of R. Yosi and even in fixed veset not concerned as stated; and all the more unfixed veset rabbinic; and further we say there when Ravin came, etc.; and that there is no proof since blood is removed we attribute to anything even though not concerned at all. Nevertheless he wrote even though so is primary — must be concerned for Rabbi's words.`,
    '34#א': `Pregnant, etc. There 9a he asked him, etc. "likewise blood," etc. — appears no examination needed at all and not concerned at all; and that which we say in Pesachim 112b "near her veset" — does not refer to pregnant. Rosh; and Tosafot HaRosh in name of Tosafot; and one can say when fetus not recognized. Tosafot HaRosh.`,
    '34#ג': `And nursing. We learn from pregnant; and as stated above 138; and likewise; and this is what is written "even if flowing," etc. as stated in baraita per R. Meir; and likewise.`,
  },
  'tiferet-yisrael': {
    '1#_': `Seif 1. See what Gaon Imrei Moshe s.k. 1 challenged — behold there are three sightings and two equal skips in a week; if so why not say veset for skipping in week; and see what he wrote; and in that seif itself Gaon was doubtful in that reasoning; and per my weak view one can resolve: it deals she was accustomed to see previously on that day of week of fixed veset and changed to see on another day of week but did not fix veset; and afterward began seeing by interval as stated; if so even Rav agrees three skips in week are needed for accustomed is different and in between she already clearly fixed interval veset — requires study.`,
    '2#_': `Seif 2 in Shulchan Aruch seif 3. If she fixed veset for hours — Raavad derives this from ascending from ritual immersion — her husband on the riverbank, etc.; and I in my poverty cannot understand this proof, for it is clear in Gemara the reason is her friend recognized her; and therefore permitted her husband on the riverbank before city entry — as Rashi and Tosafot wrote; if so one can say besides possible jumping veset — more possible they only attributed to friend's recognition; and possible Raavad did not explain so in Gemara; but the wonder Gaon Imrei Moshe wondered s.k. 3 on Mechaber who ruled uprooted at once even without examination — one can say behold Rif and Rambam and even Raavad hold husband coming from road had relations with her even while sleeping since vesetot are rabbinic; and above siman 184 reason for matter; if so in this veset contrary to majority of women who do not intend by hours and also not explicit in Talmud and poskim — Mechaber relied on those great ones who do not require even initial examination — they certainly hold here established in presumption of purity — need not even initially examine — one can say.`,
    '3#_': `Seif 3. See Gaon Imrei Moshe s.k. 9 why Mechaber omitted Rambam's view ch. 8 halachah 7 Laws of Forbidden Relations — she was accustomed to see on 15th and changed to 16th both forbidden; changed to 17th permitted 16th; changed to 18th forbidden 18th and all permitted, etc.; and Maggid Mishneh wrote even though she fixed skipping veset why 15th permitted uprooted by fixing another veset — nevertheless also concerned for 18th lest she see; and likewise Tosafot version; and left requires study; and truly great difficulty; per my view one can say Tosafot and Rambam agree to Shulchan Aruch law that if she fixes once skipping veset no further concern — only Rambam deals sight on 17th continued two days and on 18th saw without continuation as usual once and once; and even though we rule not like Ramban only we always follow beginning of sight — nevertheless Gaon already wrote s.k. 17 Tur holds like Ramban regarding skipping veset from majority is rejected — month veset is common, skipping uncommon; if so Rambam holds thus (and possibly for this Tur ruled above like Ramban without dissent since Tosafot and Rambam here hold like him) — certainly if we see she was never accustomed to extend veset two days until that 17th sight and also on 18th saw without continuation — even if we say she fixed skipping veset as we truly rule we follow beginning of sight and 15th permitted uprooted by skipping sight — nevertheless concern lest she see next month also on 18th and then clear she fixes equal month veset and we follow end of 17th sight so she can fix on 18th for common equal month; but if 18th passed and she did not see and saw on 19th — return to law we follow beginning of veset — this is Tosafot and Rambam intent concerned for 18th lest she see; if she sees on 18th certainly fixes month veset and we follow end of sight; but for Gemara law if she skipped without continuation we do not concern for 18th at all — Tosafot and Rambam agree; and no dispute at all on Gemara version and sugya; therefore no need to bring Beit Yosef their view; or Tosafot and Rambam deal if woman accustomed always to see at day beginning — no question whether before or after sunrise — then forbidden only that night and day before permitted; but Shulchan Aruch already wrote s.k. 87 if he had relations in adjacent onah and she saw attributes to her veset; and see Gaon Perishah's view attributes corruption, etc.; and Rambam holds since concern perhaps she saw previous month that day perhaps also this month — but if she certainly fixes skipping veset without doubt Tosafot and Rambam agree to Shulchan Aruch law — requires study; or plainly deals she always skipped to next day only on 17th unclear before or after sunrise and on 18th saw as usual by day — we say presumptively she fixed skipping veset and uproots first to permit 15th and 17th sight was after sunrise and habit comes in time — nevertheless Tosafot and Rambam hold still not free from concern lest she see next month on 18th and fix common month veset for perhaps still no fixed skipping veset since sight was before sunrise — why uproot fixed 15th — say from 18th for this; but if she sees next month on 18th certainly concerned and forbidden both; but for Shulchan Aruch law dealing without doubt she saw for skipping — Rambam and Tosafot agree; and this settles Hagahah "likewise" on Rambam — no need explain this is arranged Gemara; and wonder on Maggid Mishneh; truly I say even though somewhat difficult in Rambam's words essence missing — nevertheless per my view I wrote for otherwise Tosafot and Rambam words oppose mishnah and Gemara clear if she fixes skipping veset properly without doubt she no longer concerned for month veset — equal to all law she fixes four times in skipping like month veset three times — requires study; and per my view Rosh's difficulty in chapter 1 Niddah examine within veset even without veset per R. Yosi — see what Gaon wrote s.k. 26 on this in Gaon's mother's words.`,
    '4#_': `Seif 4. See Gaon Imrei Moshe s.k. 10 to resolve Rosh's contradiction Niddah to Bava Kamma where wrote regarding goring halachah like Rav — his words: truly should rule like Rav for he rules like him in prohibitions — only since vesetot rabbinic we rule leniently like Shmuel — straight reasoning; and one can say if we rule like Shmuel needing three skips — also stringency needing concern for many veset types and like my view above siman 184 examination before every relations unlike if she fixes veset like Rav in two skips — no need for this at all; nevertheless there are several corners if not fixed regarding uprooting etc. as seif 2 and requires study. But apparently one can raise how Gemara compares goring ox to veset per Shmuel needing three skips in veset — likewise in ox perhaps Shmuel himself doubts veset if two skips suffice like Rav — only since vesetot rabbinic we are lenient and require three skips; but regarding goring this presumption is Torah and full verse — if so certainly halachah like Rav; and who says goring is Torah halachah like Rav — requires study.`,
    '5#_': `Seif 5. See Gaon Imrei Moshe s.k. 26 on Shach s.k. 226 who raised if woman saw Rosh Chodesh Shevat Adar Nisan and then alternated and saw Sivan and Av — we count Nisan for fixed veset and here only twice for alternation; and Gaon challenged from Bava Kamma Gemara ox gored five six Shabbat Shabbat — first for first day we judge and established for all days or second Shabbat we judge and established only for Shabbatot — unresolved; and Rambam Laws of Monetary Damages ch. 6 wrote it is doubt; and matters similar without distinction — and in rabbinic matter doubt to leniency — if so go to leniency all sides and say she fixed alternation veset not every month — need only be concerned from two to two months, etc.; and before I raised I thought whether relevance for law per Shach who was stringent and per Gaon who proved leniency — apparently main analysis whether if Elul arrives per Shach we judge Nisan for month veset — forbidden Elul from month veset for she only skipped twice; impossible per Gaon we judge Nisan for alternation veset leniently — Rosh Chodesh permitted; but more apparently no relevance — necessarily if she sees in Elul revealed fixed first veset is common like most women saw — and now doubt only on Elul; and though young Israel for days and wisdom I am unworthy to insert head between two great mountains — nevertheless I said apparently all agree forbidden in Elul for even going lenient she fixed alternation veset per Gaon as I brought previous s.k. Rambam ch. 8 Laws of Forbidden Relations ruled certainly she fixes skipping veset nevertheless concerned for coming month lest she fix month veset; and above Gaon challenged Mechaber why omitted Rambam view for Tosafot agree impossible as stated Rambam deals doubtful skipping fixation — all agree; if so here great doubt all agree Rambam and Tosafot law forbidden forever on coming Rosh Chodesh Elul — if Rambam deals complete skipping veset here great doubt all agree Rambam and Tosafot law; if so clear forbidden in coming Elul and in Elul doubt revealed for us — but truly difficulty on Shach what relevance whether we judge Nisan fixed month veset or not — per above view Rosh Chodesh Elul always forbidden and when Elul arrives doubt revealed; and one can say if we do not judge Nisan fixed month veset per Shach — also alternation veset not judged — she is like woman without veset needing examination before relations and such must be concerned for interval etc. — one strained stringency for certainly she has veset month or skipping and otherwise certainly lenient; and per Shach s.k. 84 even woman without veset within thirty days is like woman with veset — husband need not examine; and in thirty days doubt revealed as stated; and one can say though Elul remains forbidden from concern lest fix month veset — nevertheless near her veset permitted and forbidden only that onah unlike if forbidden from fixed veset forbidden even near veset — clear above s.k. 84 must separate near veset even if saw only once; strained to divide all this if that sight early cannot attribute other veset — but in doubt place can say this sight was skipping veset and though concern lest other fixation then need separate near veset since otherwise only rabbinic and doubt to leniency — great strain; must say strained certainly impossible per Shach view it is fixed — if so when her veset passes forbidden to come without asking as above siman 184 unlike Rif and Rambam who permit even sleeping; if only from concern all agree Rambam and Rif law permit even sleeping — general "perhaps"; if we judge Nisan skipping veset and no time to see — and one can say month veset we judge nevertheless perhaps did not see and permitted — this would be Gaon's intent; but in essence no relevance — Rosh Chodesh Elul certainly forbidden lest we not be concerned for skipping doubt what Rambam and Tosafot concern even without doubt; and when Elul arrives doubt revealed if she saw we see month veset fixed; if not saw plainly she fixed skipping veset; all difference whether husband must ask or permitted without asking per Rif and Rambam — Shach's intent wrote plainly we judge Nisan month veset — if so forbidden; and wonder on him — behold unresolved doubt to leniency — need only be concerned from two to two months — plainly permitted without asking when Elul onah passes; but in essence Rosh Chodesh Eluf forbidden to have relations — Gaon agrees; one can say great relevance between them for uprooting — if she did not see on Rosh Chodesh Elul husband permitted nevertheless if she sees 20th Tishrei and on Rosh Chodesh Tishrei did not see per Shach still has fixed veset for Rosh Chodesh for not uprooted twice in order; per Gaon no uprooting needed for month veset — need twice uproot alternation veset she fixed — requires study; rejection possible too.`,
    '6#_': `Seif 6. See Gaon Imrei Moshe s.k. 17 straight reasoning to resolve Tur's words ruling here like Ramban we follow end of veset since can fix common month veset unlike above where extended; and one can say still difficulty like Rosh's difficulty beginning chapter minor girl examine at veset time even per view woman does not fix veset within veset to know extension time of veset — until uncommon veset we are not concerned and did not enact on this at all.`,
  },
  'torat-hashlamim': {
    '3#_': `Veset for hours. Such as after her immersion and similar — see Beit Yosef.`,
    '5#א': `Sometimes there will be interval. Beit Yosef wrote so explained from Rashba; and so Raavad in Sefer Baalei Nefesh daf 25b explicitly; and wrote there likewise if she skipped retroactively e.g. to 29th and then to 28th; and so Shach in name of Tosafot; and Shach further wrote likewise if she initially saw on 29th then 31st then 33rd then 36th — concerned for 39th and so forever; and this is Mechaber's intent in what he wrote whether she distanced skip, etc.`,
    '6#א': `She saw three times on Sunday. E.g. she saw on Sunday and returned and saw after three weeks on Sunday — she fixed veset for Sunday every three weeks; so Perishah Bach and Shach; and do not challenge if so why need teach this — for also fixed interval veset equally literally; one can say for interval veset would not be fixed until fourth sight because first sighting is not called interval at all unlike week-day fixation fixed after three times for first time is called Sunday as Beit Yosef wrote.`,
    '7#א': `Until she sees on 18th of Tammuz. Then there are three skips and concerned for 19th of Av and 20th of Elul and so forever.`,
    '7#ג': `And must be concerned for their words to be stringent. Bach Taz and Shach wrote this means concerned for stringency of both views i.e. concerned for 17th and 18th of Tammuz; and if fixed three times not uprooted except three times; and so Raavad in Sefer Baalei Nefesh end daf 96 — we doubt whether halachah like Rav in prohibitions or say since they dispute also regarding law here halachah like Shmuel — requires study; Rosh and Rashba also brought in Beit Yosef wrote Raavad ruled like Rav.`,
    '8#א': `And 17th of Sivan. Per first view Mechaber brought seif 7 — necessarily deals she had fixed veset initially as above; so Perishah; and this appears Tur and Mechaber intent wrote saw three times in three months skipping — implies all sights must be in skipping; if she had no fixed veset first sight in skipping is not called first sight as explained above; if so also in this law concerned for stringency of both views as s.k. 14 and Shach challenged Perishah wrote implication Tur and Rashba here both Rav and Shmuel suffice three sights — end quote; his words not compelled at all; no implication in their words at all; can explain their words as stated; and from where lenient against R. Chananel brought in Tosafot Niddah 64a s.v. itmar — clear for Shmuel even in such case need four sights; especially since this law learned from R. Chananel's words as Rashba in Tosafot HaRosh 174a wrote.`,
    '8#ב': `And concerned forever. Bach seif 11 wrote likewise three times in two months returning in cycle is also fixed veset — e.g. saw 15th Nisan 16th Iyar 15th Sivan 16th Tammuz 15th Av 16th Elul — afterward concerned 15th Tishrei 16th Cheshvan and so forever; so in Sefer Baalei Nefesh Raavad daf 96a; and that poskim stated three months not two months (see Bach and Taz to resolve this difficulty) — appears for emphasis they stated even if third-time skip three times and one might say first fixation uprooted and fixation for skip month and concerned 18th Tevet 19th Shevat and so forever — teaches nevertheless all one fixation i.e. for cycle skipping — clear.`,
    '9#_': `She fixed veset. And first sighting from count per all; as Beit Yosef in name of Baalei Nefesh Raavad — it is equal veset; as explained nearby seif 12; and plain; and so Shach; and not like Perishah and Taz.`,
    '12#_': `Alternation veset. Shach wrote therefore called alternation veset since default women default from thirty to thirty — this woman saw from two months to two months alternated from way of other women. But more appears deals even if she initially saw Rosh Chodesh Adar and then Rosh Chodesh Sivan — even though now saw month to month if she again saw Rosh Chodesh Sivan and Av she fixed alternation veset for now we see she alternated two to two months — end quote Shach; and truly his words puzzling at first sight since initial sighting was Rosh Chodesh Adar and then Rosh Chodesh Sivan — how wrote now saw month to month — behold from three months to three months; and further against Shulchan Aruch who wrote initial alternation sighting was Rosh Chodesh Nisan; per his words she never saw Rosh Chodesh Nisan. In printed Shach corrected and wrote: even if she initially saw Rosh Chodesh Iyar — but also no correction for then difficulty where alternation fixation from one alternation sight; she saw Rosh Chodesh (Nisan) Iyar Sivan and once skipped to Rosh Chodesh Av; also still against Shulchan Aruch; and more wonder on both versions how Shach concludes if she again saw Rosh Chodesh Sivan — until now deals she saw in Sivan; therefore appears primary as old Krakow editions initial sighting Rosh Chodesh Adar but where wrote and then Rosh Chodesh Sivan must emend Nisan, etc.; if so Shach's words correct — even though initially saw Adar and Nisan consecutively month to month — if afterward saw Sivan and Av — Nisan sight joins and here three skips; only if she had three-times fixation month to month then Nisan sight does not join and needs one more alternation sight to fix veset; per this Shach's words explain well — see his words at length.`,
    '13#ב': `She saw on 1st of Iyar or did not see. Bach and Perishah like Beit Yosef — if she saw on 1st of Iyar not concerned for 9th of it; and so Shach in his book Nekudot HaKesef; see Taz who extended to uphold Rabbi's view; and so clear explicitly from Raavad in Sefer Baalei Nefesh daf 56a — see there.`,
    '13#ג': `And not concerned for skipping veset, etc. How she saw 15th Nisan — so in Gemara end of chapter HaIshah and consensus of Rishonim and Acharonim as Beit Yosef above seif 11; Shach s.k. 32 wrote this is Rabbi's explanation of Ramban's words and correct even though not Beit Yosef and other Acharonim's view — end quote; I found no dispute in this — agreed by all Acharonim — only in preceding case until one uprooted, etc. — dispute in their explanations of Ramban — see Beit Yosef Darkei Moshe Bach — perhaps printing error.`,
    '13#ה': `Only 11th. For in month skipping first sighting from count; but in interval skipping in any case first sighting not from count for in every interval need four sights; nevertheless per one who holds in month skipping first sighting not from count — in interval skipping need five sights as s.k. 8; and so Taz and Shach except Shach left Rabbi's words requires study and per what I explained.`,
    '13#ו': `For we always follow beginning of sight. And what she afterward saw is extra blood added to her; if so she fixed for skipping and concerned 18th Tammuz 19th Av and so forever; and such Mechaber ruled above siman 184 seif 6; Me'adenei Melech daf 426a wondered above siman 184 seif 4 wrote woman who changes veset to advance two or three days or delay when veset arrives must separate two or three days before or after; since this contradicts what ruled we follow only after beginning of veset — and when first onah passed and she did not see permitted — end quote; see Shach what he wrote to resolve this difficulty; and truly initially requires study for not similar at all — above deals woman without fixed veset as Hagahot Maimoniyot explicit even when day thirty onah beinonis arrives her way to advance sight entirely two or three days or delay — sometimes sees at veset time — not dealing with veset continuation; therefore must separate that onah time lest she see unlike here fixed skipping veset by beginning of sight and concerned for skipping veset — clear.`,
    '14#א': `She was accustomed to see day twenty. Tur and poskim wrote per Talmud law woman does not fix veset in niddah days nor zivah days; they extended these laws; Mechaber and Rabbi omitted all this — because Tur and poskim in name of Ramban wrote since nowadays daughters of Israel were stringent not to separate niddah and zivah days — likewise for veset fixation no distinction — all plain and clear; in Nekudot HaKesef Hagahah challenged Beit Yosef and Rabbi wrote Ramban said only for stringency she fixes veset even in niddah and zivah days but not to be lenient — certainly would not dispute Talmud; already explained in several places laws of stringent unfixed from fixed; also one without fixed veset must be concerned for month veset and interval unlike fixed; and so Rashba in Tosafot HaRosh and Maggid Mishneh in name of Ramban said only to be stringent; if so Mechaber and Rabbi should have brought these laws — end quote; per my view Beit Yosef well intended — need not be so stringent in rabbinic vesetot nowadays; know main reason Rashba in Tosafot HaRosh wrote if you divide between niddah and zivah days they would need to learn gates of niddah and zivah days — appears explicitly in no case divide — clear; see s.k. 52.`,
    '14#ב': `She saw at end of 20th. Meaning this woman accustomed to interval veset from 20th to 20th — afterward changed and did not see until interval of 30th; and likewise second time did not see until 30th; and when 30th arrived did not see — only after 30th saw once; and afterward saw distant from that sight 20th — returned to first establishment even though three times did not see on day 20th — day 20th not uprooted since day 30th not fixed — if woman skips one veset two or three times and not fixed in between for another time and returns to see at veset time — first veset not uprooted until she fixes another veset (so Gemara and Rashi and Rosh intent; and Rashba in Tosafot HaRosh; and Shach in Nekudot HaKesef; Taz's wonders on Beit Yosef and Shulchan Aruch removed) — and even though even if first establishment not on 20th — interval of 30th uprooted since she changed once in interval before fixing as Shach s.k. 40 (but month veset distinction as Shach there) — nevertheless comes to teach even though did not see three times on day 20th returns to first establishment; and in Nevertheless daf 426b wrote not specifically when did not see on thirtieth third time but when interval of 30th not yet arrived — immediately after second sight on day 30th saw on interval 20th returned to first establishment and not concerned for 30th even though not yet uprooted by not seeing — nevertheless this seeing on 20th which is first establishment day counts for uprooting two sightings of 30th — end quote; see Shach who left this explanation in difficulty.`,
    '15#ג': `And likewise if she stopped from seeing three onot. So Beit Yosef explained Tur; Maharshal explained Tur's words another clear way; so Bach; and though Derishah and Taz challenged — see Nekudot HaKesef who justified all his words with good reasoning.`,
    '15#ד': `On first veset day. Meaning she should see one sighting and afterward sight at end of 20th — since uprooted and did not see three onot and day 20th itself unlike stopping once and not seeing on day 20th — though afterward not concerned for interval of 20th for no interval here since did not see at all — no month veset law; if one Rosh Chodesh passed and she did not see — concerned for next Rosh Chodesh until three Roshei Chodesh pass lest say chance she did not see this Rosh Chodesh and will see another since accustomed on Rosh Chodesh; but for interval cannot say so — for when she sees at end of 40th will not see on interval of 20th; so Maharshal Bach Shach in Nekudot HaKesef; nevertheless immediately when she again sees first sighting whenever — concerned and immediately returns to first establishment since uprooted only once unlike passing three onot must specifically return and see on day 20th itself; and Shach in Nekudot HaKesef explained Shulchan Aruch words unlike Taz who said Shulchan Aruch words imprecise — no relevance to below seif 20 regarding pregnant and nursing because there veset not uprooted only blood removed by pregnancy — immediately returned to establishment — clear.`,
    '20#_': `That yesterday's yawning causes. And no relevance to above seif 17 where we say today causes not yesterday's jump for jump is different due to coercion — so Derishah seif 60; and Taz and Maggid Mishneh end daf 298 also divided; see Mishmeret HaBayit 174a who divides explicitly; and Shach and Taz; and responsum Chut HaShani siman 14; but rejects there this division above because not found in any book; in siman 15 strains greatly to resolve this difficulty and wrote followed Beit Yosef and combined Rambam's view — certainly not per Rambam plainly she fixed veset for days not yawning for per his view does not fix at all for yawning as Maggid Mishneh ch. 8 Laws of Forbidden Relations wrote.`,
    '25#_': `Forbidden entire veset onah. So Beit Yosef in name of Rosh in name of Raavad; however above siman 184 Beit Yosef brought Raavad's view veset coming by chance whether she has fixed day etc. — likewise forbidden only for its hour; see Taz who extended to resolve; but plain language Rosh and Raavad in Sefer Baalei Nefesh is not so; Shach in Nekudot HaKesef also challenged; though strains greatly to resolve Raavad's words; but truly more appears Rosh wrote his own reasoning in this law forbidden entire onah (and Beit Yosef wrote Rosh likewise in name of Raavad because Rosh concluded at end all this Raavad's precision; but actually does not refer to this law only other laws mentioned there in Rosh (as explained in Sefer Baalei Nefesh) and not Raavad's view above; and Rabbi ruled above siman 184 seif 2 body veset dependent on bodily change — concerned only at veset hour — deals not coming at known time — clear.`,
    '28#_': `And elderly woman. See siman 164 seif 3; see Shach who wrote: know wherever this siman says she fixed veset — if for leniency it is specifically not in niddah and zivah days as Rashba Tur and poskim — end quote; already wrote above s.k. 27 so in name of Nekudot HaKesef book and rejected his words — see there.`,
    '29#א': `That elderly woman so fit. And even though she is scrupulous; and likewise if unfit to see even though not scrupulous — for matter does not depend on her as Beit Yosef in name of Yerushalmi.`,
    '34#ב': `That she encounters it. Mechaber ruled like Rashba because Beit Yosef wrote so appears from Talmud matter in reason — see there; Shach wonders on Mechaber who ruled stringently against Tur and Ramban who ruled not concerned unless she saw once.`,
  },
  'turei-zahav': {
    '7#ג': `And must be concerned for their words, etc. Wonder — for even per first view there is one stringency — if she has concern for two vesetot and one not uprooted unless second fixed as seif 13 beginning of Hagahah; if so per latter view here skipping veset fixed three times — automatically uprooted concern for second veset she had and no longer concerned; per first view not yet fixed and concerned for both too — therefore Rabbi wrote for this matter we rule like first reasoning i.e. in both be stringent — correct; and I have room to examine Tur on this who wrote Rosh ruled like first reasoning i.e. like Shmuel in Gemara not like Rav who is latter reasoning here; and in chapter Shor sheNagach 4 and 5 Rosh wrote daf 8 we rule like Rav here — requires study.`,
    '8#_': `She saw three times in three months, etc. Can state briefly e.g. 15th Sivan 16th Tammuz then 15th Av 16th Elul — she fixed afterward in one month on fifteenth and in second on sixteenth and so forever; but teaches leniency even if skip is three days i.e. 15th 15th 17th — we follow them and concerned in third month on day 17 even though between day 15 only two days; and automatically know if skip more than three days i.e. saw four times in four months three times skipping — also we follow them; stated three times for this is measure she was presumed in — automatically same law for more than this. So appears plain.`,
    '12#א': `Alternation veset first sighting, etc. Meaning she alternated Rosh Chodesh i.e. saw Rosh Chodesh Nisan Sivan Av — fixed for Rosh Chodesh alternation — afterward not concerned Rosh Chodesh Elul only Rosh Chodesh Tishrei and so forever; here Rosh Chodesh Nisan from count even per first view seif (4)[7] in interval skipping needing four sights — there we count month days how many days between first and second sight — through this interval veset recognized first and second related only to fix veset — therefore first not from count for alone has no interval relevance; but here fixation for Rosh Chodesh and also first Rosh Chodesh from count for in it alone also veset relevance since it is Rosh Chodesh; what difference whether between first Rosh Chodesh sight and second and one Rosh Chodesh between them or two — end veset specifically on Rosh Chodesh.`,
    '13#ד': `She saw on 1st of Iyar or did not see, etc. In Tur in name of Ramban it says and if she did not see, etc.; Beit Yosef wrote appears if she saw on Rosh Chodesh Iyar need not be concerned for 9th of it — reason if she returned to see on Rosh Chodesh Iyar we would say first sight on Rosh Chodesh Nisan is primary and second on 20th is extra blood — therefore not concerned for 9th Iyar nor 20th; but now she did not see on Rosh Chodesh Iyar revealed first sight on 20th Nisan is primary and concerned for 9th and 20th Iyar; Darkei Moshe disagreed wrote from nearby and concerned for both until she fixes, etc. — implies before fixing one veset three times concerned for both; and further nearby wrote she saw on 9th, etc. — implies even though saw twice for interval twenty — nevertheless concerned for month days and must be concerned 20th Iyar — likewise here even if saw on 1st Iyar must be concerned 9th from sight of 20th Nisan; and that stated did not see on 1st Iyar — appears for leniency even though Rosh Chodesh Nisan veset uprooted — nevertheless must be concerned for both twenty until uprooted once — end quote; and so appears primary; Rama well emended here saw or did not see — for we do not find anywhere sight in changed time uproots initial concern as long as no change of fixation as its law three times or four times; and further if she also sees on Rosh Chodesh Iyar and 9th and 28th — also will not fix interval twenty from 20th Nisan sight — certainly she fixed veset since three equal intervals; we do not care she also saw Rosh Chodesh Iyar; if so how permit from Rosh Chodesh Iyar sight not concerned 9th at all since possible to reach veset fixation; Perishah wrote though possible fix interval twenty from twenty — nevertheless we do not initially concern until we saw three equal intervals; difficulty — whatever possible certainly we concern lest come to that like all places this siman except skipping veset not concerned until fixed as seif 11; and clear proof from Tur end this seif saw three times Rosh Chodesh and third time on 25th of month and Rosh Chodesh — also concerned advance day lest another veset fixes — behold there clear three times Rosh Chodesh and default onah beinonis for woman — nevertheless also concerned 25th day — kal vachomer here two sights before us one 20th Nisan and second Rosh Chodesh Iyar — must say one primary and other chance — who says Rosh Chodesh primary and not concerned 9th — say 20th Nisan primary and must be concerned 9th Iyar for Rosh Chodesh Iyar blood redder than 20th Nisan — therefore appears primary as Rama's words also if saw Rosh Chodesh Iyar concerned 9th and 20th Iyar; only what Rama explained Tur's words in what wrote if she did not see — leniency does not settle for me; if so also afterward in wrote saw or did not see on 9th should also state this leniency. Rabbi exaggerated also to divide against Rama and said complete error if saw Rosh Chodesh Iyar to be concerned 9th since interrupted Rosh Chodesh Iyar sight in between — if concerned for interval twenty days must concern from Rosh Chodesh Iyar sight as Tur nearby wrote accustomed day twenty and changed day thirty both forbidden when day twenty arrives for sight of thirty forbidden — clear not concerned interval twenty from sight before thirty only concern lest see day twenty from sight of thirty she now saw — as Rav Huna son of Rav Yehoshua end chapter Benot Kutim — end quote; I say honor scholars inherit but his words are mistake before the Ruler; on contrary proof for Rama's view there we count only from sight of thirty since no sight before thirty only was fit to see day twenty initially and now changed and waited until thirty — therefore Rav Huna son of Rav Yehoshua holds not count from when fit to see only from when actually saw — unlike Rav Papa who holds count from when fit; and this plain in sugya there also from Rashi and Tosafot HaRosh extended proves if count from when fit to see — concern lest arrive shorter time than now saw and we do not say this one distanced and we concern lest advance — end quote; appears if she also saw on day she was accustomed — we see she advanced to see and certainly must be concerned day twenty from twenty sight and day twenty from thirty sight; if so also here must be concerned interval twenty days from twentieth day Iyar and from Rosh Chodesh Iyar — therefore appears plain if truly sight also now on twentieth and added to see on thirtieth plainly all agree count from twentieth sight to be concerned also interval twenty from it and we do not care she interrupted thirtieth sight to lenient her for this — therefore matter clear Moses is true and his Torah is true and his words here are widespread halachah in Israel that even if saw Rosh Chodesh Iyar it is as if she did not see for all concerns.`,
    '13#י': `11th that she is concerned for skipping, etc. Difficulty — behold from Ramban's words in Tur; Tur already wrote above in name of Ramban we rule like Shmuel needing four sights for skipping veset; Beit Yosef resolved here deals she already had veset before began seeing in skipping — in this Shmuel agrees three sights suffice as seif 7; Ramban should have explained deals woman accustomed fourteen to fourteen days and changed and saw fifteenth and continued, etc.; Derishah brings Maharshal and Rabbi same — per this Tur's conclusion concerned for days third is fixed veset and for other days unfixed skipping veset — appears skipping veset not yet fixed — end quote; I wondered on their words how wrote concerned for other days skipping veset — for since skipping not fixed as its law no concern when day fit to see by her skip until she skipped three times as its law four sights as seif 11; if Tur deals she already saw fourth time on eighteenth — behold also skipping veset fixed like fixed day seventeenth — why call only fixed day seventeenth and skipping unfixed; appears per my view Ramban himself though wrote in his name rules like Shmuel — nevertheless Ramban himself stringent for law like Rav three sights suffice as seif 7 end; proof Rosh in chapter HaIshah wrote Rambam ruled like Shmuel and also to Ramban appears so — he did not write rules for law like Shmuel as wrote regarding Rambam's view — rather appears to him so; but for practical law stringent in three forbidden; and proof Tosafot HaRosh extended wrote first R. Chananel and Raavad like Rav and wrote afterward Rambam ruled like Shmuel and Ramban wrote so appears; nevertheless wrote however concern for R. Chananel's words — end quote; from however appears Ramban himself likewise though appears like Shmuel — nevertheless concern like Rav; if say however is Rashba's language — should not write however but concern like R. Chananel; therefore necessarily Ramban himself wrote thus to be stringent practically; and one can say from Tur in name of Ramban above incident on twenty-third day, etc. — appears need four sights like Shmuel; as I stated nearby — one can say there for leniency from now on concerned only for her skip — if say she fixed skipping veset in three sights would result leniency not concerned twenty-third as stated there — therefore need four sights there then specifically go lenient unlike here when say in three sights skipping veset fixed — results stringency afterward concerned for that skip — here we can be stringent like Rav; already wrote this seif 7; and Tur's fixed day seventeenth concerned as fixed veset means like all woman's equal day veset not in skipping as Beit Yosef; per Maharshal's way should not say fixed veset with demonstrative — per my view.`,
    '14#ג': `And if after she changed, etc. Ramban's words in Tur; apparently against Talmud for so in end chapter HaIshah she was accustomed day twenty and changed day thirty both forbidden; arrived day twenty and did not see — permitted until day thirty; arrived thirty and saw; arrived twenty and did not see; arrived thirty and did not see; arrived twenty and saw — day thirty permitted uprooted at once since not fixed three times and day twenty forbidden — Rashi explained behold accustomed on twenty and uprooted only twice for last twenty after thirties she did not see — not uprooting since did not change to fortieth and did not see until day twenty for her veset; and Rosh if woman skips veset even three times and does not see in between at other time and returns to veset time — veset not uprooted until she fixes veset — end quote; if so difficulty on Ramban why wrote she changed twice to day thirty and saw on day twenty — appears still did not uproot twenty three times; Gemara we cited even if uprooted twenty three times as Rashi explained explicitly; appears to resolve Gemara deals month interval i.e. first sight on twentieth of month and change to thirtieth all in recognizable month days; therefore though passed three times not seeing twentieth of month — when saw fourth time on twentieth of month recognized habit comes in time — first veset time recognizable from month days; but Ramban here copied this law for day interval i.e. first sight from twentieth to twentieth and changed to thirtieth as stated explicitly when day thirty arrives for sight of thirty, etc.; if she said passed three times thirty and third time did not see thirtieth and afterward saw twentieth — would not be recognizable from this that first veset from twenty to twenty since before this twentieth sight now saw did not see at all only on middle thirtieth days — fifty days from sight to sight — no interval recognition she had initially; therefore needed to say she saw now twentieth after second thirtieth sight and from there recognizable twenty-day first interval; Ramban does not deal she now see two sights in a row; therefore Ramban's law she saw twentieth after second thirtieth sight and from there recognizable twenty-day interval and from this must be concerned from that twentieth sight when another twenty days arrive; and likewise if saw after third thirties once and twenty days between them — same law returned first veset to place and teaches leniency day thirty permitted though not yet uprooted since now first veset returned to place; in Tosafot HaRosh 174 explains also Talmud words above on interval days; and what Talmud said arrived thirty and did not see arrived twenty and saw — that twentieth is after thirtieth day she saw; and see there appears scribal error in his words wrote concerned for day thirty arrived thirty and did not see twentieth and saw — must emend thirtieth and saw; appears also Ramban's version in Gemara; and per this truly if did not see three times on twentieth uprooted even if did not see thirtieth and saw twentieth after those thirties; but in Rosh version like our Gemara — requires study; Beit Yosef and Shulchan Aruch did not notice this.`,
    '15#ג': `And likewise if she stopped, etc. Tur did not write likewise language but and if she stopped, etc.; Beit Yosef explained also from above i.e. passed three onot three times twenty days she was accustomed and did not see and what wrote after passed twenty days means three times twenty days — blood removed not concerned afterward — appears if before passing three onot of twenties not permitted entire twentieth day within them though did not see on second twentieth day — forbidden on third twentieth day; therefore forced to explain what Tur wrote and if she stopped refers specifically after three onot and did not see; what Tur wrote afterward returned to see, etc. — meaning on veset day as stated here in Shulchan Aruch; and Beit Yosef brought above this seif Raavad wrote nevertheless if she returned to see that day even after several stops, etc.; difficulty since proves here deals interval days as I wrote above — how find she returned to veset day — her veset in interval total days one sight joins fellow and here did not see long time and no sight to count interval; see end this discourse what I wrote from this. But Maharshal explained Tur's words here and wrote: I say reason here not because blood removed and not dealing stopped three onot only — even if stopped once entirely and did not change sights at all — no longer concerned that day forever as language plainly implies; reason not concerned day twenty here because no interval of twenty since she stopped and did not see; if we concerned day twenty would be interval forty from last sight — no reason to say that day she stopped and did not see counts as if saw — end did not see — not like changing sight to another e.g. thirtieth where concerned coming twentieth after thirty sight for fixed interval veset as above; but when not seeing at all no interval applies — therefore above where changed twentieth to thirtieth when day twenty arrives for thirty sight forbidden and not say concerned tenth day after thirty sight which is twentieth of first veset since due to come — evidently we lean to attribute to sight more than day she was fit to attribute — as Rav Huna son of Rav Yehoshua end Benot Kutim; all the more where no sight at all not attribute to what never came; therefore not concerned even onah beinonis thirty days from last sight — only woman without fixed veset we say so; but this one with fixed veset only stopped seeing fixed day — no concern day thirty after since no relevance before us; what Tur wrote returned to see concerned day twenty forever wherever stopped and returned to see returns first veset and concerned from this sight; but in stopping three onot blood removed and concerned only day twenty from this sight unlike not stopping three onot and saw — concerned also interval measure from last sight until this sight twenty thirtieth forties fifties — those passed three onot not concerned this interval since blood removed — unlike month veset if Rosh Chodesh passed and did not see concerned next Rosh Chodesh until three pass — need uproot three times; if not attribute chance did not see passed Rosh Chodesh and concerned next; but interval veset when twentieth arrived and stopped and did not see — no veset that day for interval depends on sight after it — she does not know which day intervals — not like Beit Yosef — end quote; though lion not answered and Rabbi brought Maharshal's view and praised; his explanation puzzling; one that Tur wrote returned to see whether stopped seeing or changed in unequal sights; and appears deals stopping three onot; and what wrote if stopped and did not see after day twenty passed — two versions; why said stopped duplicate language second time said after twenty passed and did not say did not see twentieth — necessarily on three onot deals stopped and did not see on twentieth and afterward stopped again three onot after day twenty passed and did not see at all; Taz's distinction between day interval and month — Tur explicitly wrote like uprooting interval so month veset — implies equal completely only this concerned for her day and that for month; Rabbi wants insert Maharshal's distinction this concerned her day meaning only if she sees on her day and month veset for month even if not see — explanation needs no contradiction; further Tur wrote at siman opening interval veset and day veset equal not uprooted fewer than three times — clear both struck together; further proof Tosafot HaRosh 174; if returned and saw when day twenty arrives concerned that day; if returned and saw also concerned other twenties; if saw fixed veset; if not saw uprooted and no longer concerned; end quote; before you plain if veset not fixed because did not see third time — not concerned afterward day twenty; but if fixed and afterward did not see on twentieth — certainly concerned when twentieth arrives; further clear proof place Rabbi brought Maharshal — proves opposite end Benot Kutim we rule Rav Huna son of Rav Yehoshua count interval twenty from day she changed i.e. day thirty not day twenty she was fit; Tosafot HaRosh 174 wrote if this one counts twentieth from time twenty she was fit — concern lest habit arrive early — not proper this one distanced and we concern lest advance — end quote; had been reasonable think interval from day fit to see only because she distanced by seeing thirty — if not see at all we would think interval from day fit; unlike Maharshal per whom impossible attribute to fit day only actual sight; further distinction Bach made — not clear per my view: for month veset if did not see Rosh Chodesh can say chance this Rosh Chodesh but on another accustomed Rosh Chodesh will see again; interval cannot say — when sees end of fortieth will not see interval twentieth — all Maharshal's words stand; what he wrote rather what Tur wrote — wonder Shulchan Aruch also stopped and afterward returned on veset day — unnecessary as he himself end seif; and Shulchan Aruch on veset day end seif imprecise as I wrote appears correct all sides plainly.`,
    '17#_': `Like unfixed veset i.e. if it occurred three times — so Shach s.k. 48 — see there; appears Raavad's view above seif 7 seif 3 if she fixed veset for hours i.e. by immersion and incident — derives from woman who saw ascending from ritual immersion; therefore ruled uprooted in one hour even without examination; but begins concerned for her hour — from this reason even though does not fix for jumps — nevertheless since presumed concerned initially like unfixed veset; per this also here if jumps though not in equal days — nevertheless were in equal hours — initially need not be concerned except that hour i.e. if jumped that hour and similar; but not before or after; Mechaber abbreviated and relied above seif 3; appears Ran in his Niddah novellae disputes — how permitted this woman to husband on riverbank — always sees ascending from ritual immersion; resolve similar to jumping veset — not fixed; difficulty behold begins concerned like unfixed since accustomed to see; Maggid Mishneh resolved Raavad there was specific hour and he commanded relations before that hour; if so disputed matter; Shach s.k. 48 if composite veset in days and jumps — concerned when veset arrives and jumped even before fixed three times — need not extend for clear in Baalei Nefesh — plain and clear if did not jump that day need not be concerned and we do not say perhaps she fixes veset for days alone like below other body veset; in Perishah s.k. 159 appears also here concerned — possible wrote per Tur's view fixes veset for jumps alone — if so jumps law equals other body veset; but for us distinction in fixation — also here can divide.`,
    '27#ד': `Except there is distinction, etc. Shach s.k. 65 wrote we do not count her onah e.g. if her onah forty to forty — nevertheless count three onot beinonis which is ninety days together; Maharshal Niddah daf 10 Gemara two in pregnancy days and one in nursing days — appears holds three onot for woman with veset is her three onot and if her onah forty days needs three times forty days — this is not and all Maharshal's words are his difficulty and his answer contradict Gemara Benot Kutim challenges per view two sources — why pause in nursing days one onah break suffices for impure source stopped and Gemara answers truly break suffices for different source afterward but why Maharshal difficulty maybe deals forty-day onah — if so also in nursing days need break for male purity blood only thirty-three days; or count onah beinonis as Shach and Maharshal — requires study.`,
    '29#א': `She does not fix, etc. Shach s.k. 73; see responsum Chasam Sofer siman 164.`,
  },
};
